# firstmate ca86a7ab - a fix-round push lands on the MR from another clone; the worker copy and the recorded pr_head both stay at the old head
$ git clone <fixture> <lab>/fixround && commit FIXROUND-E2E.md + a second E2E.md line && git push -o ci.skip origin HEAD:fm/nm-gl-e2e
$ glab mr view 4 -R gh0stwin/firstmate-gitlab-port-fixture -F json | jq -r .sha   # live MR head
58d01a1e705fa74d3a23a85ac76a32f76cf30b0e
$ grep ^pr_head= state/nm-gl-e2e.meta   # recorded at arm, now stale
pr_head=58d01a1e705fa74d3a23a85ac76a32f76cf30b0e
$ git -C <worktree> rev-parse HEAD   # local branch, also stale
58d01a1e705fa74d3a23a85ac76a32f76cf30b0e
$ git -C <worktree> cat-file -e <live head>   # the worker copy has never seen the fix-round commit
absent (as expected)

